Niloy Talukder is a Research Assistant of Civil and Environmental Engineering at the University of Windsor, Canada. He received the Master’s degree in civil engineering from the University of Windsor. Mr. Talukder has conducted research on the development of warning strategies for partially-automated driving.
Chris Lee, Ph.D., P.Eng. is a Professor of Civil and Environmental Engineering at the University of Windsor, Canada. He received the Ph.D. in civil engineering from the University of Waterloo, Canada. His research interests include vehicle interaction and conflicts in car-truck mixed traffic and manual-autonomous vehicle mixed traffic, carfollowing and lane-changing behaviour, driver safety in partially-automated vehicles, advanced real-time speed control for freeways, and aggressive and distracted driving.
Yong Hoon Kim, Ph.D., P.Eng. is an Associate Professor of Civil and Environmental Engineering at the University of Windsor, Canada. He received the Ph.D. in civil engineering from Purdue University, U.S.A. His research interests include advanced driver assistance systems, connected and autonomous vehicles, intelligent transportation systems, advanced traveler information systems, transportation system analysis and modeling, and traffic flow modeling and simulation.
Balakumar Balasingam, Ph.D., P.Eng. is an Associate Professor of Electrical and Computer Engineering at the University of Windsor, Canada. He received the PhD in electrical engineering from McMaster University, Canada. His research interests include autonomous (cyber, physical and human) systems, signal processing, machine learning, and information fusion.
Francesco Biondi, Ph.D. is an Associate Professor of Kinesiology at the University of Windsor, Canada. He received the Ph.D. in experimental psychology from the University of Padova, Italy. His research interests include human factors in manufacturing and transportation, workload assessment, and user-centered design.
Aditya Subramani Murugan is a Ph.D. student of Industrial Engineering at the University of Windsor, Canada. His research interests include computer vision, neural networks, and gamification.
Eunsik Kim, Ph.D., P.Eng. is an Assistant Professor of Industrial Engineering at the University of Windsor, Canada. He received the Ph.D. in industrial engineering from Pennsylvania State University, U.S.A. His research interests include occupational ergonomics, ergonomic intervention, physiological measurement and analysis, biomechanics, musculoskeletal disorders, and manual material handling.
